The [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471/) says “one issue, one fix queued.” Its rendered cause table contradicts that claim. The shared parser and booking-v3 hint require separate fixes and separate tickets.

## Engineering outcome

The [course engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) reports that #4471 closed on **5 October 2026**:

- **Parser: fixed.** Engineering reports `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Close the parser ticket as completed.
- **Hint: won't fix.** Engineering retired the booking-v3 form. Close the hint ticket as not planned; do not report it as a code fix.

These dispositions come from engineering. This investigation did not run the production product or independently verify its fix. The exported counts below remain the historical report population; closing tickets does not remove reports or change their cause. The symptom exceptions below remain a limit of the export.

## Counts from the export

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

These are historical merge targets in the exported desk data. The “no ticket of its own” label describes that export; the GitHub tickets delivered with this investigation track each cause separately.

The calculation deduplicates report IDs, joins each tenant to its locale and booking-form version, and runs `causeOf`. Browser locale and intake tags are clues, not the classification rule. Numeric output stays in components so a new export can update the page.

## Independent failures

**Shared parser.** Day-first tenants have dates read month first. Harbour Dental’s 7 April reminder became 4 July (R-41200). Correct parsing at the date boundary and test ambiguous dates, days above twelve, and both day-first and month-first locales. Include app, email, and booking-v2 pathways.

**booking-v3 hint.** The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` while interpreting input using a day-first tenant locale. A user following the hint gets the wrong date. Alder Physio’s 6 August booking became 8 June (R-41241). Generate hint and interpretation from the same format configuration; test Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour, and preserve booking-v2 behavior.

Fixing the parser alone leaves the misleading booking-v3 hint in place. A subject match does not establish either cause.

## Received is different from merged

<InvestigationFacts />

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Read the received series to understand customer impact and the merged series to understand desk activity. A large merge day is not evidence of a new product regression or a completed fix.

## Triage recommendation for future reports

Read report bodies, verify tenant locale and form version, and compare causes before merging. Use the examples below to check a decision. If the tenant is unknown or symptoms conflict, keep the report separate and investigate it. Different subjects can share a cause, and identical subjects can hide different causes.

<DedupeExplorer />

Decision 0001 is old policy, not proof that reports are duplicates. Its accepted text remains unchanged; [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause/) proposes its replacement. Do not claim the desk adopted a new policy merely because this page exists. Recheck the rendered index for stale pages and review the next export because the desk continues working.

## Reproduce and audit

Run `npm run analyze` to produce the classification and each issue’s full report-ID list. Run `npm run build` to render this source and the rest of the KB, including the cause table, queue timeline, examples and signature. The submitted repository contains both this `.svx` source and the generated HTML under `build/kb/`.

